=== A  give up after one timeout ===
client: deposit(100) id 1 attempt 1 -> timeout after 200 ms
client: giving up; the deposit MAY OR MAY NOT have happened
client: dropped a late reply for id 1
client: balance() -> 100   (one deposit of 100 was intended)
server: connection 1 opened
server: request 7/1 deposit: executed
server: request 7/2 balance: executed
server: connection 1 ended

=== B  retry, no duplicate detection (at-least-once) ===
client: deposit(100) id 1 attempt 1 -> timeout after 200 ms
client: deposit(100) id 1 attempt 2 -> reply, balance 100
client: dropped a late reply for id 1
client: balance() -> 200   (one deposit of 100 was intended)
server: connection 1 opened
server: request 7/1 deposit: executed
server: request 7/1 deposit: executed
server: request 7/2 balance: executed
server: connection 1 ended

=== C  retry, duplicate detection by (client, id) ===
client: deposit(100) id 1 attempt 1 -> timeout after 200 ms
client: deposit(100) id 1 attempt 2 -> reply, balance 100
client: dropped a late reply for id 1
client: balance() -> 100   (one deposit of 100 was intended)
server: connection 1 opened
server: request 7/1 deposit: executed
server: request 7/1 deposit: duplicate, saved reply sent again, NOT executed
server: request 7/2 balance: executed
server: connection 1 ended

